---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii4_237",
  "series": "Band II 4 (1701 - 1707)",
  "seq": 237,
  "text": "<p> [[714.1]] <b>237. BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES FÜR LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[714.2]] [Hildesheim, 23. Dezember 1707]. [236.238.] </b></p>\n<p> [[714.10]] Antonius Perez in 2^#'d^#'a^#'m 2^#'d^#'a^#'e Tract. IV. disputatione VI, caput 3. De Augmento charitatis. </p>\n<p> [[714.11]] 1. Duae sunt difficultates hic a nobis per angustias temporis brevissime attingendae. Prima\n[[714.12]] difficultas est utrum actibus remissis, et duratione libera actus caritatis augeatur meritorie\n[[714.13]] caritas. Existimo partem affirmantem satis aperte colligi ex sess. 6. Trident. cap. 10 et 16 et\n[[714.14]] Canone 24. Sed solet hic negotium facessere objectio quaedam vulgaris sumpta ex eo quod\n[[714.15]] videatur sequi ex qualibet duratione actus charitatis infinitum augmentum charitatis; nam in\n[[714.16]] ultimo instanti V. G. durationis aliquis gradus charitatis datur in praemium; at in quolibet\n[[714.17]] instanti praecedente datus est alius aut plures gradus non minores illo: cum ergo instantia sint\n[[714.18]] infinita, gradus acquisiti aequales erunt infiniti. </p>\n<p> [[714.19]] Omitto aliorum solutiones, quarum aliae negant infinitatem in continuo, aliae concessa\n[[714.20]] infinitate negant existere in continuo puncta et momenta actualia; aliae negant continuam\n[[714.21]] libertatem durationis, aliae dicunt in singulis momentis solum produci indivisibile praemii et\n[[714.22]] quasi punctum. Sed nos ne de his rebus quaestionem faciamus, admittimus continuam libertatem\n[[714.23]] durationis et disputationis gratia infinitatem momentorum, et in singulis momentis\n[[714.24]] acquiri plusquam indivisibile praemii. </p>\n<p> [[714.25]] Respondeo itaque ex propria sententia, plerosque authores in hac re latuisse quoddam\n[[714.26]] principium: est autem illud, quantitatem charitatis et qualitatis intensae non esse unicae dimensionis.\n[[714.27]] Quantitatem unicae dimensionis voco in qualitate illam quae est proportionalis lineae et\n[[714.28]] tempori; si enim quantitas qualitatis proportionalis lineae ponatur in loco et extendatur, solum\n[[714.29]] occupabit unam lineam spatii: quando autem potest occupare, si extendatur, locum correspondentem\n[[714.30]] superficiei tunc dico esse duplicis dimensionis, et esse proportionalem superficiei,\n[[715.1]] quando autem potest occupare locum solidum, tunc dico esse trinae dimensionis et proportionalem\n[[715.2]] corpori. Dico ergo concedi posse quolibet momento augeri charitatem augmento proportionali\n[[715.3]] lineari quantitati, et licet augeatur in singulis momentis aequaliter, inde solum sequi\n[[715.4]] augmentum finitum proportionale superficiei finitae continentis lineam infinities. Sic si charta\n[[715.5]] illuminetur a sole successive, ita ut in primo momento temporis illuminatur linea prima chartae,\n[[715.6]] et in sequentibus successive illuminentur caeterae, donec tota charta in fine temporis maneat\n[[715.7]] illuminata, non sequitur superficiem illuminatam seu quantitatem lucis extensam esse infinitam\n[[715.8]] in ratione superficiei, sed solum sequitur continere infinitas lineas sicut linea continet infinita\n[[715.9]] puncta, quod juxta sententiam continui quam supponimus, non censetur absurdum. </p>\n<p> [[715.10]] Si quid autem absurdum est in sententia nostra, tota absurditas consistit in suppositione\n[[715.11]] affirmante infinitam multitudinem punctorum actualium aut instar mathematicorum in quantitate\n[[715.12]] et tempore, quam ego existimo esse impossibilem etiam de potentia absoluta; nam licet\n[[715.13]] continuum sit in infinitum divisibile ut ego existimo et infinita contineat indivisibilia metaphysica,\n[[715.14]] mathematica tamen actualia non potest continere infinita actu sed solum in potentia.\n[[715.15]] Quomodo autem differat indivisibile metaphysicum, et indivisibile mathematicum actuale, et\n[[715.16]] indivisibile mathematicum potentiale alibi explicui; et in hac dinstinctione existimo consistere\n[[715.17]] solutionem difficultatis continui; sed ut dixi ad hunc locum non spectat haec quaestio. Sufficit\n[[715.18]] ostendisse ex affirmatione meriti durationis actus caritatis nullam difficultatem novam oriri\n[[715.19]] contra naturam continui. </p>\n<p> [[715.20]] Hucusque Ant. Perez. Caetera in eodem capite contenta non spectant ad hanc materiam. </p>\n",
  "number": "237.",
  "title": "BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES FÜR LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "[Hildesheim, 23. Dezember 1707]. [236.238.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:237. BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES FÜR LEIBNIZ [Hildesheim, 23. Dezember 1707]. [236.238.] Antonius Perez in 2^#'d^#'a^#'m 2^#'d^#'a^#'e Tract. IV. disputatione VI, caput 3. De Augmento charitatis. 1. Duae sunt difficultates hic a nobis per angustias temporis brevissime attingendae. Prima difficultas est ut...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>